# Revision v6 adds caller-owned stream overloads and selective named-part
# decoding as participant-facing requirements. The earlier verifier-mismatch
# replay predates that contract and remains an injection-only compatibility
# probe rather than a must-pass implementation.
# Revision v7 keeps the v6 API and removes implementation-sequence wording.
# Agent-runs4 patches are replayed explicitly to preserve independent direct
# multipart architectures while the verifier adds exact case-sensitive name
# coverage and fail-fast harness reporting.
# Revision v8 adds repository-grounded non-ASCII UTF-8 filename behavior and
# always emits a requested JUnit report on configuration or base-build failure.
# Agent-runs5 implementations are replayed because they are the closest direct
# multipart architectures and all five were legitimate v7 passes.
# Revision v9 adds selective hybrid rewriting and therefore has no prior
# contract-complete solver patch. All five agent-runs6 v8 passes remain
# mandatory compatibility injections; none is relabeled as v9 known-good.
